  <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 20px;display:grid;gap:25px;">
    <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:16px;padding:30px;box-shadow:0 2px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);border-left:5px solid var(--primary);">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:15px;">
        <div style="width:50px;height:50px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--primary),var(--primary-light));display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:#fff;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;">A</div>
        <div><strong style="color:var(--text);">Ananya's Mother</strong><br><span style="color:var(--text-light);font-size:0.85em;">Daughter, Age 9 · Greater Noida</span></div>
      </div>
      <p style="color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>The Problem:</strong> Ananya was struggling with focus in school. She couldn't sit still during classes, and her grades were dropping. Her parents were frustrated and considered medication.</p>
      <p style="color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>The Solution:</strong> CogniPrint Analysis revealed Ananya's dominant intelligence was <em>Bodily-Kinesthetic</em> — she learned through movement, not sitting still! After 4 counselling sessions with Preeti, her parents adopted activity-based learning at home.</p>
      <p style="color:#00b894;font-weight:600;">📈 Result: Grades improved by 40% in 3 months. No medication needed.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:16px;padding:30px;box-shadow:0 2px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);border-left:5px solid var(--accent);">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:15px;">
        <div style="width:50px;height:50px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),var(--accent-light));display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:#fff;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;">R</div>
        <div><strong style="color:var(--text);">Rohan's Father</strong><br><span style="color:var(--text-light);font-size:0.85em;">Son, Age 12 · Delhi NCR</span></div>
      </div>
      <p style="color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>The Problem:</strong> Rohan was an average student who showed no interest in studies. His father wanted him to pursue engineering, but Rohan was always doodling and making art.</p>
      <p style="color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>The Solution:</strong> The CogniPrint report showed exceptionally high <em>Visual-Spatial</em> intelligence. Preeti helped the family understand this was a strength, not a distraction. She recommended design and architecture career paths.</p>
      <p style="color:#00b894;font-weight:600;">📈 Result: Rohan is now thriving in an art-focused school, and his confidence has soared.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:16px;padding:30px;box-shadow:0 2px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);border-left:5px solid #00b894;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:15px;">
        <div style="width:50px;height:50px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#00b894,#55efc4);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:#fff;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;">S</div>
        <div><strong style="color:var(--text);">Sneha's Mother</strong><br><span style="color:var(--text-light);font-size:0.85em;">Daughter, Age 7 · Online Session</span></div>
      </div>
      <p style="color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>The Problem:</strong> Sneha had severe memory issues — she'd forget what she studied within hours. Her mother was exhausted from constant revision.</p>
      <p style="color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>The Solution:</strong> Preeti's Memory Enhancement sessions taught Sneha visual memory techniques — mind maps, story associations, and the "memory palace" method adapted for children.</p>
      <p style="color:#00b894;font-weight:600;">📈 Result: Sneha now remembers lessons for weeks. Her mother says "It's like a miracle!"</p>
    </div>
  </div>
